IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ita-types`
IMPORT `ita-rates`

-- Properties of the Second Schedule's rates for a resident individual from the year of assessment 2024 (Table 3), as checked and proved.
--
-- WHY A RESTATEMENT: `l4 prove` decides `#ASSERT`s over symbolic inputs with the z3 solver, but its fragment does not take a LIST, so it cannot read
-- `the tax by bands` (`ita-rates.l4`), which walks a list of bands. `the Table 3 tax on` below is the same table written out as one BRANCH, with the
-- tax at each band's start worked out by hand from the Act's bands; two things tie it to the encoding:
--   1. evaluation: the two agree at every band edge, one dollar either side of it, and at four points past the top edge;
--   2. both are continuous and piecewise linear with the same twelve edges, so agreement at the edges and at one point of the open top band, where
--      the slope is fixed, is agreement everywhere.
-- The proofs themselves, over every chargeable income, are in sg-household-tests-proofs.l4 (run with `l4 prove`, not `l4 run`).
--
-- Source: Second Schedule Part A, Table 3 (YA 2024 and later), ../source/ITA1947.txt.

§ `Table 3 as one BRANCH`

GIVEN c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Table 3 tax on` MEANS
    BRANCH IF c AT MOST 20000 THEN 0
                      IF c AT MOST 30000 THEN 0 PLUS (c MINUS 20000) TIMES 2%
                      IF c AT MOST 40000 THEN 200 PLUS (c MINUS 30000) TIMES 3.5%
                      IF c AT MOST 80000 THEN 550 PLUS (c MINUS 40000) TIMES 7%
                      IF c AT MOST 120000 THEN 3350 PLUS (c MINUS 80000) TIMES 11.5%
                      IF c AT MOST 160000 THEN 7950 PLUS (c MINUS 120000) TIMES 15%
                      IF c AT MOST 200000 THEN 13950 PLUS (c MINUS 160000) TIMES 18%
                      IF c AT MOST 240000 THEN 21150 PLUS (c MINUS 200000) TIMES 19%
                      IF c AT MOST 280000 THEN 28750 PLUS (c MINUS 240000) TIMES 19.5%
                      IF c AT MOST 320000 THEN 36550 PLUS (c MINUS 280000) TIMES 20%
                      IF c AT MOST 500000 THEN 44550 PLUS (c MINUS 320000) TIMES 22%
                      IF c AT MOST 1000000 THEN 84150 PLUS (c MINUS 500000) TIMES 23%
                      OTHERWISE 199150 PLUS (c MINUS 1000000) TIMES 24%

§ `Tied to the encoding by evaluation`

GIVEN c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the encoding's tax on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the resident individual rates for YA` 2026 `on chargeable income of` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST t THEN t

#ASSERT (`the Table 3 tax on` 0) EQUALS (`the encoding's tax on` 0)
#ASSERT (`the Table 3 tax on` 1) EQUALS (`the encoding's tax on` 1)
#ASSERT (`the Table 3 tax on` 19999) EQUALS (`the encoding's tax on` 19999)
